+# Maintain the generated skill pack
+
+This guide contains repository mechanics that users do not need to install the skills.
+
+## Environment and generation
+
+The package and unit tests support Python 3.11+. Byte-for-byte generation uses Python 3.13.7 as
+pinned in `.python-version` and `corpus.yaml`; `uv` provisions it.
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-groups
+uv run google-guides all
+```
+
+`all` syncs pinned sources, builds public skills, regenerates the catalog and token report, and
+validates the result. Run `uv run google-guides all --include-swe-book` for the local-only
+SWE-book release check. Hosted CI uses synthetic restricted-source fixtures and does not generate
+the book derivatives.
+
+Other maintenance commands are:
+
+```text
+google-guides sync                         clone and checkout pinned repositories
+google-guides build [--collection ID]     build selected redistributable skills
+google-guides build --include-swe-book     also build SWE-book skills locally
+google-guides catalog                      regenerate catalog files
+google-guides metrics [--include-swe-book] measure generated text
+google-guides validate [--include-swe-book] validate output and license boundaries
+google-guides eval triggers                plan skill-selection tests
+google-guides eval quality                 plan comparative answer tests
+```
+
+## Checks
+
+```bash
+uv run ruff format --check src tests
+uv run ruff check .
+uv run pytest --cov=google_guide_skills --cov-report=term-missing
+uv run google-guides all
+git diff --exit-code -- skills catalog
+```
+
+Change `corpus.yaml` or the generator rather than hand-editing generated prose. Keep source changes,
+tests, generated outputs, and license evidence together. Do not add a source whose distribution
+rights are unclear, commit `.generated/skills/`, or redistribute local-only output.
+
+The package is intended to run from a source checkout. Build metadata marks it private, and wheels
+exclude generated guide trees and do not contain an initialized corpus.
